<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    The SIMULATOR build uses this file, not Daak.entitlements. It carries the
    App Group because the iOS 26 simulator data protection keychain grants
    access ONLY to a process whose adhoc signature carries an access group.
    This file is selected with
      CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS[sdk=iphonesimulator*]
    so Daak.entitlements (the DEVICE build) stays free of the App Group and a
    free-team sideload .ipa still installs.

    ponytail: measured on the iPhone 17 simulator (5E019877), iOS 26.2. The
    keychain read for onboarding.v1 returned -34018 with an empty entitlements
    file. keychain-access-groups SIGKILLed the app at exec (SBMainWorkspace
    denied the launch), with or without a team prefix, with or without
    application-identifier and com.apple.developer.team-identifier. Only this
    key made the read succeed. Remove this key and the -34018 banner returns.
    The DEVICE build must NOT carry it: a free team grants no App Group.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
  <array>
    <string>group.dev.darshit.daak</string>
  </array>
</dict>
</plist>
